    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d337">

                <pb facs="0408" n="1142" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1142"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Baron von thielmann.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging your note of the 22d instant,
                    I have the pleasure to inform you that your present request has been anticipated
                    by an instruction sent to the consul-general of the United States at Apia,
                    Samoa, under date of June 17 last, wherein he was directed to act in accordance
                    with the propositions contained in Mr. Gresham’s note to you of April 18
                    last.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
